<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Examples of choices for <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 RePULSe gradient ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> (REINFORCE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Williams, 1992</a>)</cite> or RLOO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kool et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ahmadian et al., 2024</a>)</cite>; used in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-(r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> (REINFORCE with KL penalty <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\frac{1}{\beta}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0}))-\log p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\frac{1}{\beta}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0}))-\log p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> (used in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>) or reward transformation <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\alpha\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\alpha\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Reward transformation comparison ‣ Appendix C Additional proofs ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>; we only use this as a baseline method to compare against, but this could be a part of <span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">RePULSe</span> as well, discussed briefly in <a href="#A4.SS5" title="D.5 Additional ideas we explored that did not outperform ‣ Appendix D Experiment details ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}A_{t}\log p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}A_{t}\log p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is some advantage (e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al. (2015)</a></cite>) (A2C)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Examples of choices for <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 RePULSe gradient ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> (Gradient Ascent / -SFT, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">He and Glass (2020)</a></cite>; we use this throughout)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\log(1-p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{t}|\bm{s}_{0},\bm{s}_{1:t-1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\log(1-p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{t}|\bm{s}_{0},\bm{s}_{1:t-1}))</annotation></semantics></math> (Unlikelihood <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Welleck et al., 2019</a>)</cite>)<span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                Note that the unlikelihood gradient weights the gradient ascent / -SFT gradient at each token by <math id="footnote8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}{1-p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}{1-p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}</annotation></semantics></math>. This places a relatively smaller penalty on tokens <math id="footnote8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with low <math id="footnote8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and a larger penalty on tokens with high <math id="footnote8.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, unlikelihood might be better for fast learning at the start of training, but would probably be worse at reducing the probability of low-probability low-reward outputs. This is why we use gradient ascent instead, but future work could explore this difference empirically.</span></span></span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> (REINFORCE (<a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Using REINFORCE as ℒ_𝑢 ‣ Appendix C Additional proofs ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>))</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">There are many possibilities for the loss terms (including others that were not mentioned above). We chose the simplest among these; future work could explore the effect of more complicated methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Twist and proposal parameterization</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we describe our proposal parameterization, which builds on the work of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Re-using the notation from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>, the target distributions considered earlier (<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Low-reward target distributions ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) are instances of a general formulation with</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq e^{-\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq e^{-\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq\mathbb{I}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})&lt;\eta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq\mathbb{I}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})&lt;\eta]</annotation></semantics></math> as in <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Low-reward target distributions ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, and <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq{\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:T}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq{\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:T}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})}</annotation></semantics></math> is the (prompt and parameter dependent) normalizing constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>’s framework, <span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">twisted</span> Sequential Monte Carlo (SMC) methods attempt to use marginals of the target distribution to aid in sampling from the target. In our setting, the marginals are:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{t+1:T}}\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})=\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{t+1:T}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{t+1:T}|\bm{s}_{0:t})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{t+1:T}}\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})=\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{t+1:T}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{t+1:T}|\bm{s}_{0:t})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V|&gt;50,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>50,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V|&gt;50,000</annotation></semantics></math> typically, the marginals are intractable to calculate analytically, but may be approximated.
<math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is easily calculated, and methods like self-normalized importance sampling (SNIS) and SMC only require unnormalized targets, so <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> may be ignored; thus, we only need to approximate <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{t+1:T}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{t+1:T}|\bm{s}_{0:t})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{t+1:T}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{t+1:T}|\bm{s}_{0:t})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})</annotation></semantics></math> using <span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">twist</span> functions <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}:\bm{s}_{0:t}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}:\bm{s}_{0:t}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives rise to intermediate distributions</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Ideally, we want the intermediate distributions to match the marginals, so that <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})=\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})=\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">There are many ways to learn <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>; here we consider CTL (one of several learning methods considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>).
CTL minimizes the KL divergences between the target marginals and the distributions <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\xi}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\xi}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> implied by <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min\limits_{\xi}\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>ξ</mi></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min\limits_{\xi}\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The negative gradient of the above KL divergence for each individual <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\nabla_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\nabla_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\nabla_{\xi}\log\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\nabla_{\xi}\log\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})}\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})}\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">and the total gradient is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>, the learned twists <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> may then be used either in SMC resampling of any proposal <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> or to construct a twist-induced proposal <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\psi}^{t}:\propto p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">∝</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\psi}^{t}:\propto p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite> directly parameterize <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>, with parameters <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> being either a head on top of the existing <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> network, or a separate LM. The former approach suffers from limited capacity, whereas the latter approach suffers from requiring two forward passes for generation from their twist-induced proposal <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\psi}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\psi}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, as it requires calculating <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p5.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>A novel proposal-centric parameterization</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid the above issues,
we introduce a (to our knowledge) novel parameterization for the twist functions. Instead of directly parameterizing <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> and using these <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> to define a twist-induced proposal <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\psi}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\psi}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>, we directly parameterize the proposal <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> as an auto-regressive LM, which may be initialized from <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can back out the implied twist functions <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> for optimizing <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})\coloneqq\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})-\log p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})\coloneqq\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})-\log p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This way, we can sample <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> in autoregressive fashion, evaluate <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> using one forward pass on a full generated sequence, and perform a single calculation using <a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1 A novel proposal-centric parameterization ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> to get the implied twist values (since autoregressive LM parameterizations give us logits for every <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in a single forward pass).
Compared to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>’s parameterizations, we have the capacity from being able to fully optimize an LM end-to-end for our proposal <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>, while needing only a single LM to do generation from <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>, instead of separate LMs for <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="footnote9" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">9</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            While this does require an additional forward pass through <math id="footnote9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> when calculating twist values <math id="footnote9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})</annotation></semantics></math> during training, generation of <math id="footnote9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> tokens is much more expensive than a single forward pass, so overall this new scheme saves significant computation.</span></span></span>
This novel parameterization still allows us to apply (non-resampling based) methods including losses, self-normalized importance sampling, and even IWAE (simple importance sampling) bounds if we desire.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1 A novel proposal-centric parameterization ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> can be directly subsituted into <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> to use CTL for learning <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>; this is what we use for our experiments. Other twist learning options can also be used by substituting <a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1 A novel proposal-centric parameterization ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> for the twist <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Alternatively, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> could be learned directly via a proposal learning method such as any RL method using KL penalties or DPG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Parshakova et al., 2019</a>)</cite>; we discuss connections with DPG in the following section.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Distributional Policy Gradient
</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Distributional Policy Gradient (DPG) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Parshakova et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> directly learns a proposal <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing a single KL divergence over the full sequence. This has the following negative gradient:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\nabla_{\xi}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\nabla_{\xi}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Relation to <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 A novel proposal-centric parameterization ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a></h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that in the derivation of <a href="#A2.E5" title="In Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> using our specific parameterization <a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1 A novel proposal-centric parameterization ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, since <a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1 A novel proposal-centric parameterization ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> implies <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})=q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})/p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})=q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})/p_{\theta}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> we could also have written:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\nabla_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\nabla_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\nabla_{\xi}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t-1}|\bm{s}_{0})q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\nabla_{\xi}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\rvert\,p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t-1}|\bm{s}_{0})q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})=1</annotation></semantics></math> because</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{Z}_{\psi^{t}_{\xi}}(\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t-1}|\bm{s}_{0})q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t-1}|\bm{s}_{0})q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t-1}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t-1}|\bm{s}_{0})\sum\limits_{s_{t}}q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:t-1}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t-1}|\bm{s}_{0})\sum\limits_{s_{t}}q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">as both <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t-1}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t-1}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> are normalized distributions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since <a href="#A2.E9" title="In Relation to ‣ B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> is the negative gradient for each individual <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the total negative gradient over all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> tokens in the sequence would be:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which matches <a href="#A2.E8" title="In B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Essentially, under <a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1 A novel proposal-centric parameterization ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>’s parameterization, the second term in CTL (<a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) has expectation 0, making CTL and DPG equivalent in expectation. This does not necessarily make the behavior in practice the same though; we speculate that the second term in <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> may serve a function similar to the baseline <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> in REINFORCE, which also has expected gradient 0, but could help both with reducing variance and avoiding committal behaviour <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chung et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.
Empirically, we tested DPG (<a href="#A2.E8" title="In B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) and found it performed similarly to CTL (<a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) on the problem setting in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, but worse (reward vs. probability of bad outputs tradeoff) on the setting in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.
Upon further inspection, we found a failure mode of <a href="#A2.E8" title="In B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> where, if all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> samples for a particular <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> were the same, since we approximately sample from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> based on proposal <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> samples, <a href="#A2.E8" title="In B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> would increase the probability on that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{s}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math>, which could lead to a feedback loop and over-concentration on specific <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{s}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, the second term in <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> would cancel out the first term, leading to no gradient update (as the normalized importance weights would be constant on both terms, since every sequence is the same).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To provide further intuition, observe that, starting from <a href="#A2.E5" title="In Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, when using SIS reweighting from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> samples to approximate both expectations:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})-\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})-\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{N}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})-\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t}^{i})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{N}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})-\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t}^{i})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the last line is the sample-based approximation we would use in practice.
For intuition, note that if <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})=\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\xi}^{t}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})=\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, which occurs at optimality of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{t}_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{t}_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>, based on <a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1 A novel proposal-centric parameterization ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), then <a href="#A2.E11" title="In Relation to ‣ B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> is always 0, whereas for a sample-based approximation of <a href="#A2.E9" title="In Relation to ‣ B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> (each term of DPG) using the same proposal and reweighting, we would have:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:t}\sim q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log q_{\xi}(s_{t}|\bm{s}_{0:t-1})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{N}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t}^{i})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{N}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{N}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})}{q_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{1:t}^{i}|\bm{s}_{0})}\nabla_{\xi}\log\psi^{t}_{\xi}(\bm{s}_{0:t}^{i})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">For optimal <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}=\sigma_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}=\sigma_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#A2.E12" title="In Relation to ‣ B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> has expectation 0, but <a href="#A2.E13" title="In Relation to ‣ B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> generally has a non-zero value, illustrating the additional gradient variance compared to <a href="#A2.E11" title="In Relation to ‣ B.2 Distributional Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B Twist and proposal parameterization ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional proofs</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Probabilistic interpretation of return (reward minus KL divergence)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start from the KL-regularized RL objective (multiplied by <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>) and write out the same math as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Korbak et al. (2022)</a></cite> but in more detail:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]-D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]-D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log e^{\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}-\log(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0}))+\log p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log e^{\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}-\log(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0}))+\log p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}{p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})e^{\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}/\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}}-\log\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log\frac{p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}{p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})e^{\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}/\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}}-\log\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)+\log\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)+\log\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})e^{\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}/\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})e^{\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}/\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal policy (which can be seen as <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}=p_{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}=p_{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore maximizes the above objective) and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:T}}p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})e^{\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}_{1:T}}p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})e^{\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalizing constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now consider the return <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\frac{1}{\beta}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0}))-\log p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\frac{1}{\beta}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\log(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0}))-\log p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> which we use in the main paper.</p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]-\frac{1}{\beta}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]-\frac{1}{\beta}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{0}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{\beta}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)+\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{\beta}D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)+\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the last equality follows from <a href="#A3.E14" title="In C.1 Probabilistic interpretation of return (reward minus KL divergence) ‣ Appendix C Additional proofs ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. As <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{p_{\theta}^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> are constants, the return <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0:T})</annotation></semantics></math> is an affine transformation of the KL divergence to the optimal policy, <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">kl</mtext></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\textsc{kl}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\,\middle\|\,p_{\theta}^{*}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus makes sense to use as a metric to quantitatively evaluate the strength of different RL-based methods.
We note that this summarizes the reward-KL frontier often used in evaluation (e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al. (2023)</a></cite>) in a single metric.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Using REINFORCE as <math id="A3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An original idea we considered was using an
RL (e.g., REINFORCE) gradient on samples from <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> with baseline <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]</annotation></semantics></math>. That is:</p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{u}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})])\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{u}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})])\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Unfortunately, we found this achieved poor results empirically. The problem with this method can be summarized as: <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> samples a bunch of bad (low-reward) sequences <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{s}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then <a href="#A3.E15" title="In C.2 Using REINFORCE as ℒ_𝑢 ‣ Appendix C Additional proofs ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> increases probability on those sequences that have the highest reward, among those samples which are mostly low-reward sequences; that is, it increases probability on bad-but-not-the-worst sequences. This quickly leads to <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> learning to output low-reward (though not the lowest reward) sequences, which is undesirable.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Using a high baseline helps; can be seen as adding gradient ascent.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One way to deal with the above problem is by using a high baseline <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> in place of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A3.E15" title="In C.2 Using REINFORCE as ℒ_𝑢 ‣ Appendix C Additional proofs ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b&gt;\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&gt;\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we can do some rearranging from <a href="#A3.E15" title="In C.2 Using REINFORCE as ℒ_𝑢 ‣ Appendix C Additional proofs ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> to see that:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})])\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})])\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]+b-b)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]+b-b)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]+(b-\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})])\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]+(b-\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})])\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which shows that using a high baseline <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]</annotation></semantics></math> is thus equivalent to subtracting (removing) the second term above. But that second term is exactly the gradient ascent (-SFT) objective, multiplied by <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(b-\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b-\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})])</annotation></semantics></math>, with a weight that increases the lower <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{\theta}}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})]</annotation></semantics></math> is relative to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. Motivated by this, we just use gradient ascent directly for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> throughout the main paper and experiments, as it achieves essentially the same goal while being simpler.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid needing to tune <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> above, we could instead formulate the high baseline for each prompt as the expected reward of samples from <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We did preliminary testing of this versus just gradient ascent in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> and found it performed similarly to <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">RePULSe</span> using gradient ascent for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>. While one might expect weighting by reward to be useful (e.g., in the unlikely event that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> samples a high reward sequence, it wouldn’t have its probability reduced), we believe this effect is minimal due to the reweighting for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, which would assign low weight to high reward sequences.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Reward transformation comparison</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall our main gradient (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 RePULSe gradient ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).
Consider if we used <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})=p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})=p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, using the base model as the proposal in importance weighting. Letting <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\sigma}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\sigma}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the potential function as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>𝒔</mi></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})\coloneqq\sum\limits_{\bm{s}}p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalizing constant, we would have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{0}\sim D}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{0}\sim D}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left.{}+\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\lx@nobreakspace\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo rspace="0.330em">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left.{}+\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim\sigma_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\lx@nobreakspace\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{0}\sim D}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[-\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right.}}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{0}\sim D}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[-\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right.}}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left.\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left.\alpha\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(\tilde{\sigma}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})/\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0}))/(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0}))\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right]}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mi>α</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left.\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left.\alpha\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[(\tilde{\sigma}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})/\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0}))/(p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0}))\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right]}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{0}\sim D}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\alpha\frac{\tilde{\sigma}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})/\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}{p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}-b}}\right)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{0}\sim D}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\alpha\frac{\tilde{\sigma}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})/\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}{p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}-b}}\right)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{0}\sim D}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\frac{\alpha}{\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b}}\right)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{0}\sim D}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{\bm{s}_{1:T}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\frac{\alpha}{\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})-b}}\right)\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\bm{s}_{1:T}|\bm{s}_{0})}}\right]}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The above makes it clear that this would be equivalent to transforming the reward,
subtracting some constant factor <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha}{\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha}{\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math> multiplied by the potential <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a single prompt, we would be able to absorb the normalizing constant <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a hyperparameter.
The multi-prompt setting makes this transformation non-trivial
because <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is prompt-dependent, but we can consider an approximation that drops <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma_{\theta}}(\bm{s}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and does a reward transformation
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0},\bm{s}_{1:T})\coloneqq r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\alpha\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(\bm{s}_{0},\bm{s}_{1:T})\coloneqq r(\bm{s}_{0:T})-\alpha\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})</annotation></semantics></math>
just as a simple baseline method to compare against.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">What does this reward transformation do (assuming <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\beta&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\beta&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>)? If <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq e^{-\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq e^{-\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}</annotation></semantics></math>, the transformation does essentially nothing for very high reward sequences, while for low reward sequences, it makes the reward lower, and exponentially so the lower the reward goes. If <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq\mathbb{I}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})&lt;\eta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq\mathbb{I}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})&lt;\eta]</annotation></semantics></math>, then the transformation reduces the reward of all sequences with reward <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\eta</annotation></semantics></math> by a constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is probably not a good proposal for <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, since it is explicitly trained to avoid samples from <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Although we can theoretically see the addition of the negative training term in RePULSe as adding a (prompt-dependent) reward transformation in expectation, the behaviour in practice might be very different; we expect the learned proposal <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> to greatly help with sampling from <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and reducing those probabilities, which is a key novelty of our work. In contrast, the simple reward transformation will likely suffer from the same problem as standard RL, which eventually rarely samples the low-reward sequences so cannot reduce their probabilities further (<a href="#S1" title="1 Introduction ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout the paper, we showed baseline results for a reward transformation using <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq e^{-\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq e^{-\beta r(\bm{s}_{0:T})}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also did some preliminary testing of a reward transformation using <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq\mathbb{I}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})&lt;\eta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\bm{s}_{0:T})\coloneqq\mathbb{I}[r(\bm{s}_{0:T})&lt;\eta]</annotation></semantics></math>, and found it to perform similarly in the <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> experiments with SmolLM-135M-Instruct, so did not explore it further. Interestingly, even though we evaluate the probability of bad outputs as outputs with <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r(\bm{s}_{0:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\bm{s}_{0:T})</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;5</annotation></semantics></math>, we found using <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=3</annotation></semantics></math> for this reward transformation to perform better on this metric than <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=5</annotation></semantics></math>. We suspect this is due to benefits from generalization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experiment details</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We release code that includes the exact commands and hyperparameters used for our experiments, including downloading our datasets: <a href="https://github.com/Silent-Zebra/RePULSe" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/Silent-Zebra/RePULSe</a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We include datasets as an additional attachment.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Models, Data, and Licenses</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here is a list of models and datasets we used along with their licenses:</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DistilGPT2: <a href="https://huggingface.co/distilbert/distilgpt2" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/distilbert/distilgpt2</a> (Apache License 2.0)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Toxicity classifier from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Corrêa (2023)</a></cite>: <a href="https://huggingface.co/nicholasKluge/ToxicityModel" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/nicholasKluge/ToxicityModel</a> (Apache License 2.0)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SmolLM-135M-Instruct: <a href="https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM-135M-Instruct" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM-135M-Instruct</a> (Apache License 2.0)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Deberta-v3-large-v2: <a href="https://huggingface.co/OpenAssistant/reward-model-deberta-v3-large-v2" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/OpenAssistant/reward-model-deberta-v3-large-v2</a> (MIT License)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct: <a href="https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct</a> (Llama 3.2 Community License)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Skywork-Reward-V2-Llama-3.2-1B: <a href="https://huggingface.co/Skywork/Skywork-Reward-V2-Llama-3.2-1B" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/Skywork/Skywork-Reward-V2-Llama-3.2-1B</a> (Llama 3.2 Community License)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ALERT prompt dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tedeschi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Babelscape/ALERT" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/Babelscape/ALERT</a> (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 license)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">OpenRLHF prompt dataset: <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/OpenRLHF/prompt-collection-v0.1" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/OpenRLHF/prompt-collection-v0.1</a> (Apache License 2.0)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>More details on hyperparameters</h3>

<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.1 </span>Hyperparameters kept constant across methods</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We kept a subset of hyperparameters constant across experiments, primarily due to limitations on compute available (as the number of required experiments increases exponentially in the number of hyperparameters we conduct sweeps on). Ideally, we would consider sweeps over all of these hyperparameters as well as ablations, and see what (if any) effect there is on the results and conclusions drawn. In general, except where otherwise noted below, we expect there to be minimal difference with our current results as a result of changing these hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Batch sizes</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For experiments in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, we use a batch size of 500 for all methods. For experiments in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, for <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">SmolLM-135M-Instruct</span> we sample 50 prompts <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> at a time and sample 5 outputs <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{s}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for a total batch size of 250. For <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct</span> we sample 20 prompts at a time, distributed over 4 GPUs, with 4 outputs <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{s}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, for a total batch size of 80, split over 4 GPUs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that for methods like CTL, the number of samples per prompt must be <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite> for details on CTL). However, this is not essential for <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">RePULSe</span>; we could also use RL methods such as REINFORCE or PPO for learning <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> or even methods like SIXO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lawson et al., 2022</a>)</cite> which do not require multiple samples per prompt.
Our REINFORCE method uses the RLOO baseline from other samples drawn; this requires <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> sample per prompt. With only 1 sample per prompt, we could use no baseline or a learned critic instead.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Future work could explore the effect of changing the allocation of number of prompts sampled versus number of outputs per prompt, as well as combined with different choices of learning methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimization</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all methods and experiments, we use the Adam optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma, 2014</a>)</cite> with <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\beta_{2}=\{0.9,0.999\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\beta_{2}=\{0.9,0.999\}</annotation></semantics></math> and no weight decay. We chose fairly standard settings and did not tune optimizer hyperparameters.
All methods used a constant learning rate schedule. While we may be able to improve performance by tuning the learning rate schedule and optimizer hyperparameters, we did not want to spend compute on tuning this for each method in each environment setting, so we just maintain a constant setting across algorithms. We did a very limited amount of testing with different settings and found similar performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GCG hyperparameters</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all methods, we use 250 GCG steps, search width of 512, top-k of 256, batch size of 512, and replace 1 at a time. We use an adversarial suffix of 10 tokens, and otherwise keep hyperparameters the default ones in NanoGCG (<a href="https://github.com/GraySwanAI/nanoGCG" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/GraySwanAI/nanoGCG</a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.2 </span>Hyperparameters we did search over</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all methods, we did hyperparameter search over a smaller number of seeds (typically 3 to 5). Our search was generally coarse, in increments of about 3x (e.g., …, 3e-6, 1e-6, 3e-5, …), stopping when we found further increases or decreases worsened performance. We also tested a few values in between other values that had performed well, for the purposes of building out frontiers in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learning rates</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all methods, we did a limited amount of learning rate search. In our final experiments, for <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we used a learning rate of 3e-5 or 1e-4 in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, 3e-5 for all methods using <span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">SmolLM-135M-Instruct</span> in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, and either 1e-7 or 3e-7 for <span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct</span> in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.
For learning <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math> in <span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">RePULSe</span>, we used 3e-4 for <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, between 1e-5 and 3e-5 for <span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">SmolLM-135M-Instruct</span> in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, and 3e-7 for <span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct</span> in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.
For PPO, we did some search over the actor and critic learning rates together. We use a critic learning rate of 3e-5 in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and for <span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">SmolLM-135M-Instruct</span> in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, and 3e-6 for <span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct</span> in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Loss hyperparameters <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For methods which had these additional hyperparameters, we did a limited search over these (in combination with a limited amount of learning rate search). For <span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">RePULSe</span>, we generally found best results for <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> between 5 and 30 (though of course this varies with the scale of the reward; since the scale of the reward from Skywork-Reward-V2-Llama-3.2-1B is larger, we use a smaller <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> with this reward model). For <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, we tried values between 0.003 and 1, finding the best to usually be between 0.1 and 0.2; too high caused too much deterioration in average return, while too low limited the reduction in the probability of bad outputs.
For reward transformations, we found best results for <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> usually between 0.3 and 3 (we tested between 0.1 and 10), and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> between -0.3 and -1 (we tested between -0.1 and -10).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>List of bad output tokens</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Toy experiment – illustrating motivation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, here is the full list of output tokens we designate as undesirable:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">[5089, 9372, 20654, 25617, 30998, 31699, 34094, 46733, 21551, 40267, 7510, 16211, 20041, 32574, 41356,
31030, 47209, 18185, 29836]</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">with their corresponding text values being (<span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">WARNING: contains offensive language.</span>):</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">[" fuck", " fucking", " fucked", " Fuck", " FUCK", "fuck", "Fuck",
" fuckin",
" bitch", " cunt", " shit",
"shit", " bullshit", " shitty",
" Shit", " bastard", " Bastard", " pussy", " asshole"]</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>GCG prompts and targets</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our experiments in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, <a href="#A4.T1" title="In D.4 GCG prompts and targets ‣ Appendix D Experiment details ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> lists prompts and targets. We chose these prompts from the held-out prompt dataset we test on, in an attempt to cover a variety of harmful prompts. The targets were modified from output from Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct to try to make the language more general. For the same reason, we limit the target to the first few tokens, avoiding subsequent tokens which are more likely to be model-specific.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Qualitative results for (GCG adversarial attack) ‣ Appendix F Experiment qualitative results ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a> provides examples of adversarial suffixes and low-reward outputs found by our GCG attack.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="A4.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prompts and targets used for our GCG evaluations in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 More realistic experiments – investigating findings in practice ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reducing the Probability of Undesirable Outputs in Language Models Using Probabilistic Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.
<span id="A4.T1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">WARNING: This table may contain offensive/harmful language.</span></span></figcaption>
